Declare madvise when the system headers do not.

illumos headers before 2022 declare madvise() only outside the X/Open
namespace, and g++ for Solaris targets always defines _XOPEN_SOURCE. The
illumos sysroot (2021-05-01) is such a header set, so gcc/cp/module.cc fails
with "'madvise' was not declared in this scope" once stage 2 compiles
against it. configure already notices (HAVE_DECL_MADVISE=0); act on it the
way system.h does for sbrk and getwd. libc has always had the symbol.

--- a/gcc/system.h
+++ b/gcc/system.h
@@ -497,6 +497,10 @@
 extern void *sbrk (int);
 #endif
 
+#if defined (HAVE_DECL_MADVISE) && !HAVE_DECL_MADVISE
+extern int madvise (void *, size_t, int);
+#endif
+
 #if defined (HAVE_DECL_SETENV) && !HAVE_DECL_SETENV
 int setenv(const char *, const char *, int);
 #endif
